Q: Mapperly from Linq join ignores subsequent object property mapping A: <p>Your current scenario is suggested as in this <a href="https://github.com/riok/mapperly/issues/1978" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Mapperly GitHub issue</a> but unfortunately there is no update on this feature.</p>
<p>However, you can work with <a href="https://mapperly.riok.app/docs/configuration/existing-target/#merge-objects" rel="nofollow noreferrer">merging the objects</a> and implement your own mapping logic to merge with multiple sources.</p>
<p>Your <code>TheDtoMapper</code> class should be as below:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>[Mapper]
public partial class TheDtoMapper
{
    public partial TheDTO MapAToDto(A a);
    public partial void MergeBToDto(B b, TheDTO dto);

    public TheDTO Map(A a, B b)
    {
        var dto = MapAToDto(a);

        MergeBToDto(b, dto);

        return dto;
    }
}
</code></pre>
